1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

﻿1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
- www.MY-SUBS.com -

2
00:00:07,541 --> 00:00:10,874
Let the Harfoots be your sole concern.

3
00:00:10,875 --> 00:00:13,582
I will see to the Istar myself.

4
00:00:13,583 --> 00:00:16,249
The Dark Wizard found his staff.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:19,332
The time has come for you to find yours.

6
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:21,832
Unless there is somewhere
else you wish to be.

7
00:00:21,833 --> 00:00:22,915
Nori.

8
00:00:25,208 --> 00:00:27,082
Unless I find her soon, she will die.

9
00:00:27,083 --> 00:00:28,749
Both of them will die.

10
00:00:28,750 --> 00:00:30,874
Your friend or your destiny?

11
00:00:30,875 --> 00:00:32,291
The choice is yours.

12
00:00:33,416 --> 00:00:35,541
There's something under the mines.

13
00:00:37,750 --> 00:00:39,415
A nameless evil.

14
00:00:39,416 --> 00:00:40,915
You mustn't dig!

15
00:00:40,916 --> 00:00:43,494
We have barely taken a thimble

16
00:00:43,495 --> 00:00:46,082
from the ocean of her riches.

17
00:00:46,083 --> 00:00:48,916
Your father, he turned
his axe on my men.

18
00:00:49,666 --> 00:00:51,707
You take that army to Eregion now,

19
00:00:51,708 --> 00:00:54,541
and Khazad-dûm might not
be here when you return.

20
00:00:58,041 --> 00:00:59,332
I'm Estrid.

21
00:00:59,333 --> 00:01:01,332
Fancy you never want
for water on your island.

22
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:03,582
In Númenor, we have
water in most of our homes.

23
00:01:03,583 --> 00:01:04,832
I'd like to see that.

24
00:01:04,833 --> 00:01:06,750
I wager your betrothed would too.

25
00:01:12,333 --> 00:01:15,124
The Valar have deemed her...

26
00:01:20,458 --> 00:01:21,915
Innocent!

27
00:01:21,916 --> 00:01:24,707
Hail Tar-Míriel, Queen of the Sea!

28
00:01:24,708 --> 00:01:27,208
Hail Queen Míriel. Hail!

29
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:34,207
Once the Deceiver
obtains a being's trust,

30
00:01:34,208 --> 00:01:37,082
he gains the ability to
sculpt their very thoughts.

31
00:01:37,083 --> 00:01:38,707
Fighting at your side...

32
00:01:38,708 --> 00:01:40,957
- I felt...
- I felt it, too.

33
00:01:40,958 --> 00:01:43,249
You have already been affected once.

34
00:01:43,250 --> 00:01:46,707
Yes. He knows my mind. And I know his.

35
00:01:46,708 --> 00:01:49,082
Which is why I must face him.

36
00:01:49,083 --> 00:01:50,999
You cannot face him alone.

37
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:53,999
The High King believes I may
be vulnerable to deception.

38
00:01:54,000 --> 00:01:55,624
And why would he think that?

39
00:01:55,625 --> 00:01:56,625
Stop it, Elrond.

40
00:01:57,291 --> 00:02:00,500
Nine Rings to enslave the world of Men.

41
00:02:01,041 --> 00:02:03,583
As he... enslaved me.

42
00:02:04,250 --> 00:02:06,790
- I want the Nine!
- No!

43
00:02:06,791 --> 00:02:08,999
They will be far from your reach by now.

44
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:12,499
Then you are going to bring them
to me and place them in my hand.

45
00:02:12,500 --> 00:02:15,124
Together, this crown and your Rings

46
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:18,333
would be powerful enough to
truly destroy Sauron forever.

47
00:02:18,833 --> 00:02:20,790
Sauron has no army of his own.

48
00:02:20,791 --> 00:02:22,916
Attack!

49
00:02:23,583 --> 00:02:25,707
So he's lured yours here instead.

50
00:02:26,750 --> 00:02:28,750
He wants you to attack Eregion.

51
00:02:31,708 --> 00:02:33,166
This is all his design!

52
00:02:34,333 --> 00:02:36,291
This is what Sauron wants!

53
00:03:13,041 --> 00:03:14,125
It's the Ring.

54
00:03:14,916 --> 00:03:18,458
It has him, mind and soul.

55
00:03:22,125 --> 00:03:23,457
Get him to the healing chamber.

56
00:03:23,458 --> 00:03:25,083
What are you gonna do?

57
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:29,874
No matter what you hear, do
not follow me down that mine.

58
00:03:29,875 --> 00:03:30,958
Durin.

59
00:04:11,166 --> 00:04:12,375
Take off the Ring!

60
00:04:17,125 --> 00:04:18,500
I said, take it off!

61
00:04:18,501 --> 00:04:21,375
Or I'll take off the whole hand!

62
00:04:33,666 --> 00:04:35,833
You're strong enough to wield an axe.

63
00:04:38,500 --> 00:04:42,125
But are you strong enough to
use it against your father?

64
00:04:45,458 --> 00:04:49,291
No, Father. I'm not.

65
00:04:53,708 --> 00:04:55,708
You've always been stronger than me.

66
00:05:01,875 --> 00:05:06,375
Do you remember when I was a
wee lad, and we'd arm wrestle?

67
00:05:07,541 --> 00:05:13,541
You'd let me lift my hand, just
enough, to think maybe I could win.

68
00:05:14,791 --> 00:05:17,041
And then you'd slam it down again.

69
00:05:17,666 --> 00:05:23,625
And I knew there was nothing
stronger than my father.

70
00:05:25,375 --> 00:05:27,250
Be strong again, Father.

71
00:05:28,333 --> 00:05:30,958
Take it off. I beg you.

72
00:05:35,000 --> 00:05:39,208
A Dwarf... should never beg.

73
00:05:43,458 --> 00:05:44,458
No!

74
00:05:59,041 --> 00:06:00,875
Come and see, my son!

75
00:06:02,166 --> 00:06:05,458
Come and see the true
wealth of our mountain.

76
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,333
Behold.

77
00:06:21,166 --> 00:06:23,166
The dynasty of Durin.

78
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:48,583
But to see our mountain the way I do,

79
00:06:49,291 --> 00:06:52,583
you have to wear a ring, my son.

80
00:06:56,625 --> 00:06:59,041
It's not our mountain, Father.

81
00:07:00,791 --> 00:07:02,625
You taught me that.

82
00:07:03,291 --> 00:07:07,708
With these Rings, it could be.

83
00:07:29,416 --> 00:07:30,416
Run.

84
00:07:31,166 --> 00:07:32,333
Run, Father!

85
00:08:12,416 --> 00:08:13,999
Durin.

86
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,832
Durin!

87
00:08:15,833 --> 00:08:17,208
Durin.

88
00:08:42,250 --> 00:08:47,375
I never let you lift
your hand. It was you.

89
00:08:48,541 --> 00:08:51,625
Just you. Getting stronger.

90
00:09:01,458 --> 00:09:03,000
Forgive me, my son.

91
00:09:05,083 --> 00:09:06,291
King Durin.

92
00:09:18,916 --> 00:09:21,124
No! No!

93
00:09:21,125 --> 00:09:22,125
No!

94
00:11:50,291 --> 00:11:51,375
Huh.

95
00:12:18,666 --> 00:12:21,375
Manwë promised you would come.

96
00:12:22,250 --> 00:12:25,999
I confess, my patience wavered,

97
00:12:26,000 --> 00:12:30,958
but my faith in you,
old friend, did not.

98
00:12:31,458 --> 00:12:32,624
You know me?

99
00:12:32,625 --> 00:12:36,124
Know you? We are as kin.

100
00:12:36,125 --> 00:12:39,000
Five of us, there were.

101
00:12:39,875 --> 00:12:42,332
But you were the one who convinced me

102
00:12:42,333 --> 00:12:45,915
to leave the Uttermost
West for this world,

103
00:12:45,916 --> 00:12:49,915
because you knew none of us

104
00:12:49,916 --> 00:12:53,666
could ever hope to defeat Sauron alone.

105
00:12:55,208 --> 00:12:58,125
But I was told you wish to
ally yourself with Sauron.

106
00:12:59,791 --> 00:13:04,374
You journeyed to Rhûn
seeking answers, old friend.

107
00:13:04,375 --> 00:13:08,291
Follow me. And you shall have them.

108
00:13:09,083 --> 00:13:12,540
Your past, your name.

109
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,333
Even your staff.

110
00:13:17,875 --> 00:13:22,582
I did not make the journey
alone. Two halflings gave me aid.

111
00:13:22,583 --> 00:13:27,415
Yes. Elanor Brandyfoot
and Poppy Proudfellow.

112
00:13:27,416 --> 00:13:29,290
You need not worry.

113
00:13:29,291 --> 00:13:33,499
I have seen to it, the
small ones are safe.

114
00:13:33,500 --> 00:13:34,916
Come!

115
00:13:39,291 --> 00:13:40,332
Poppy! Nori!

116
00:13:40,333 --> 00:13:43,749
I instructed they were not to be harmed.

117
00:13:43,750 --> 00:13:45,135
They won't be,

118
00:13:45,136 --> 00:13:48,791
once you have given us
all that we were promised.

119
00:13:50,958 --> 00:13:52,582
Forgive me, old friend.

120
00:13:52,583 --> 00:13:56,040
I thought these nomads
might help me find you.

121
00:13:56,041 --> 00:14:02,040
I see now I was foolish to
place trust in such low company.

122
00:14:02,041 --> 00:14:06,666
My people were once Kings, wizard.

123
00:14:13,375 --> 00:14:14,749
Go!

124
00:14:14,750 --> 00:14:15,833
Go now!

125
00:14:17,291 --> 00:14:19,291
We tried to find you.

126
00:14:19,500 --> 00:14:21,958
My dear friends.

127
00:14:23,708 --> 00:14:26,375
Is he the fella you were
looking for out here all along?

128
00:14:29,333 --> 00:14:31,291
Dark Wizard?

129
00:14:32,625 --> 00:14:36,790
That is a name I do not embrace.

130
00:14:36,791 --> 00:14:39,749
Placed upon me by Men long ago,

131
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:43,749
out of ignorance and fear of our kind.

132
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:48,833
I hope my actions today will
lead you to know better of me.

133
00:14:52,166 --> 00:14:53,999
This the sort of action you mean?

134
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:57,166
You pity him whose
blade was at your throat?

135
00:14:57,833 --> 00:14:58,833
Yes.

136
00:15:00,416 --> 00:15:03,958
Pity will not defeat Sauron.

137
00:15:06,666 --> 00:15:10,166
And if you were to defeat
Sauron, would that suffice?

138
00:15:11,083 --> 00:15:13,750
Or would you seek to
become his successor?

139
00:15:14,583 --> 00:15:20,125
Walk with me, and in time, we
will both be his successors.

140
00:15:27,791 --> 00:15:30,332
I would sooner walk
this desert forevermore,

141
00:15:30,333 --> 00:15:32,250
nameless and forgotten.

142
00:15:36,416 --> 00:15:38,750
Then you give me little
choice, old friend.

143
00:15:48,875 --> 00:15:50,332
Everybody out!

144
00:15:52,916 --> 00:15:55,832
I only hope losing
those you care for most

145
00:15:55,833 --> 00:16:01,165
will give you a taste of the
suffering all Middle-earth will know,

146
00:16:01,166 --> 00:16:03,791
should Sauron prove victorious.

147
00:16:04,500 --> 00:16:05,541
No!

148
00:16:07,250 --> 00:16:12,541
When your senses have
returned, I will be waiting.

149
00:16:28,416 --> 00:16:30,250
Nori! Nori.

150
00:17:01,166 --> 00:17:05,000
We expect answers. What
is the meaning of this?

151
00:17:05,125 --> 00:17:07,374
I was ordered only to gather you here.

152
00:17:07,375 --> 00:17:09,082
I've no answers to give.

153
00:17:20,541 --> 00:17:21,916
Leaders of The Faithful.

154
00:17:26,083 --> 00:17:28,915
I thank you all for
coming at this late hour.

155
00:17:28,916 --> 00:17:30,083
To what end?

156
00:17:31,041 --> 00:17:34,874
We have learned why Míriel
was able to bewitch the sea.

157
00:17:34,875 --> 00:17:38,540
It would seem she has an
ally of cunning powers.

158
00:17:38,541 --> 00:17:42,207
An ally who has already
bruised Númenor once

159
00:17:42,208 --> 00:17:46,125
and is now gathering
strength to make us bleed.

160
00:17:46,708 --> 00:17:48,000
Absurd.

161
00:17:48,541 --> 00:17:54,291
The Sea Queen has no allies
but the Valar who uphold her.

162
00:18:08,916 --> 00:18:10,332
Sauron?

163
00:18:10,333 --> 00:18:14,500
All so-called Faithful are now declared

164
00:18:15,416 --> 00:18:18,207
traitors of Westernesse!

165
00:18:23,708 --> 00:18:26,750
As of this hour, all loyal Númenóreans

166
00:18:26,751 --> 00:18:29,000
are called upon to oppose this threat.

167
00:18:38,833 --> 00:18:39,833
Traitor!

168
00:18:43,375 --> 00:18:45,000
Pharazôn, you cannot do this!

169
00:18:48,416 --> 00:18:49,625
Come on, traitor.

170
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:25,916
Father!

171
00:19:26,833 --> 00:19:28,000
Father, please.

172
00:19:30,208 --> 00:19:32,000
There's no time to explain.

173
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:35,125
They're coming for you.

174
00:19:39,625 --> 00:19:41,750
Check in there. Clear them out.

175
00:19:47,375 --> 00:19:49,332
Are there any Faithful in there?

176
00:19:49,333 --> 00:19:50,666
No. Move along.

177
00:19:51,250 --> 00:19:52,250
Hm.

178
00:19:53,208 --> 00:19:55,540
Shall I tell Ar-Pharazôn
of your insolence?

179
00:19:55,541 --> 00:19:58,333
Do not resist. Don't push back. Move!

180
00:20:01,416 --> 00:20:03,041
Move along.

181
00:20:03,666 --> 00:20:04,666
Hm.

182
00:20:06,666 --> 00:20:10,875
Right. All of them. And
up there too. All of it.

183
00:20:19,500 --> 00:20:22,957
We must leave for the West.
There are Faithful there.

184
00:20:22,958 --> 00:20:24,707
My son Anárion amongst them.

185
00:20:24,708 --> 00:20:27,333
I know a ferryman who can
get us outside the city.

186
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,832
You must travel only by night.

187
00:20:30,833 --> 00:20:33,583
The stars shall be your friends
and make safe your steps.

188
00:20:36,625 --> 00:20:37,833
And yours.

189
00:20:40,541 --> 00:20:42,666
One does not need eyes
to lead in the dark.

190
00:20:48,916 --> 00:20:51,207
What cowardice have I ever
shown to make you think

191
00:20:51,208 --> 00:20:53,957
I would even consider
making safe my own skin

192
00:20:53,958 --> 00:20:55,583
at the peril of yours?

193
00:20:56,166 --> 00:20:59,666
My place is here. You know it is.

194
00:21:00,708 --> 00:21:05,125
Then where is mine, if not with you?

195
00:21:07,416 --> 00:21:09,666
It is called Narsil.

196
00:21:27,250 --> 00:21:28,583
The white flame.

197
00:21:33,708 --> 00:21:35,707
Reclaim your Lordship.

198
00:21:35,708 --> 00:21:39,416
And with this sword, your destiny.

199
00:22:53,958 --> 00:22:54,958
Go!

200
00:22:59,166 --> 00:23:01,375
There's no way out, Elf.

201
00:23:04,458 --> 00:23:05,749
This way.

202
00:23:05,750 --> 00:23:06,833
Mama.

203
00:23:37,875 --> 00:23:39,666
I'm the one your Lord-father wants.

204
00:23:40,625 --> 00:23:43,666
Set them free. And I will go willingly.

205
00:23:44,291 --> 00:23:46,457
Give me one reason, Elf.

206
00:23:49,166 --> 00:23:50,708
I will give you Nine.

207
00:24:33,833 --> 00:24:36,165
Look what you have done to yourself.

208
00:24:48,833 --> 00:24:50,500
They will be here any moment.

209
00:24:51,375 --> 00:24:53,875
Have you ever seen Orcs
in the heat of combat?

210
00:24:54,416 --> 00:24:56,041
A frenzy comes over them.

211
00:24:57,250 --> 00:24:58,666
A blood-hunger.

212
00:24:59,625 --> 00:25:05,124
When Gondolin fell, they
say it went on, and on.

213
00:25:08,166 --> 00:25:09,583
For weeks.

214
00:25:10,166 --> 00:25:11,740
Tell me where you have hidden the Rings.

215
00:25:11,741 --> 00:25:14,583
And I will end your suffering now.

216
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:19,291
It must be nearly noontide.

217
00:25:20,916 --> 00:25:25,541
One used to hear the
kingfishers, flying to the river.

218
00:25:28,083 --> 00:25:32,625
It is a pity how you have silenced them.

219
00:25:34,083 --> 00:25:36,124
All I have done has been for you.

220
00:25:36,125 --> 00:25:40,124
Yours was the fire that
crafted the marvels of the age.

221
00:25:40,125 --> 00:25:43,416
I wish only to share
them with the world.

222
00:25:46,416 --> 00:25:47,625
Please.

223
00:25:49,750 --> 00:25:50,833
Let me.

224
00:25:52,791 --> 00:25:54,791
But the Rings are beyond your reach.

225
00:25:55,583 --> 00:25:57,958
As I shall be, ere long.

226
00:25:58,958 --> 00:26:02,083
For soon I shall go to
the shores of the morning.

227
00:26:04,458 --> 00:26:09,208
Borne hence, by a wind
that you can never follow!

228
00:26:30,291 --> 00:26:32,291
There are ways of keeping you alive.

229
00:26:33,875 --> 00:26:35,083
Friend.

230
00:26:37,250 --> 00:26:40,416
Must I show you my mastery
of that craft as well?

231
00:26:41,458 --> 00:26:43,000
Craft.

232
00:26:45,125 --> 00:26:47,290
Your only craft is treachery.

233
00:26:47,291 --> 00:26:52,166
So pure, it shall betray
the very hand that forges it.

234
00:26:52,833 --> 00:26:55,707
Your words are empty.

235
00:26:55,708 --> 00:26:57,041
No.

236
00:26:58,208 --> 00:27:01,125
No, hear me. Hear me!

237
00:27:03,500 --> 00:27:05,541
Shadow of Morgoth.

238
00:27:07,083 --> 00:27:10,125
Hear the dying words of Celebrimbor.

239
00:27:11,833 --> 00:27:16,166
The Rings of Power shall destroy you.

240
00:27:17,250 --> 00:27:21,290
And in the end, I foresee,

241
00:27:21,291 --> 00:27:26,041
one alone shall prove your utter ruin!

242
00:27:33,625 --> 00:27:36,333
You're wrong. I am their creator.

243
00:27:38,375 --> 00:27:39,791
I am their master.

244
00:27:41,416 --> 00:27:42,416
No.

245
00:27:44,750 --> 00:27:48,583
You are their... prisoner.

246
00:27:49,750 --> 00:27:53,500
Sauron, Lord...

247
00:27:56,666 --> 00:27:58,333
... of the Rings.

248
00:28:35,875 --> 00:28:39,000
Are you him? Are you Sauron?

249
00:28:41,791 --> 00:28:43,583
I have many names.

250
00:28:55,250 --> 00:28:59,333
What is yours, Uruk?

251
00:29:31,625 --> 00:29:34,958
Ill fortune... to
pack a dagger in a bag.

252
00:29:36,708 --> 00:29:38,500
Say it cuts a journey short.

253
00:29:40,416 --> 00:29:42,208
This one's already stabbed me once.

254
00:29:44,375 --> 00:29:46,041
I'd wager the damage is done.

255
00:29:54,791 --> 00:29:56,041
How do you live with it?

256
00:29:57,333 --> 00:29:58,958
Had a good healer stitch me up.

257
00:30:03,458 --> 00:30:05,666
I meant, 'bout your mum.

258
00:30:08,625 --> 00:30:09,875
I heard what you said.

259
00:30:10,708 --> 00:30:12,583
About it being your fault and all.

260
00:30:14,125 --> 00:30:15,958
I wanted to know how you carry it.

261
00:30:19,791 --> 00:30:20,875
Poorly.

262
00:30:23,291 --> 00:30:24,915
I've carried it poorly.

263
00:30:24,916 --> 00:30:27,082
I didn't realize that until I came here.

264
00:30:27,083 --> 00:30:28,416
Why?

265
00:30:29,333 --> 00:30:31,750
Seems there's grander
things here than I thought.

266
00:30:33,250 --> 00:30:35,583
Enough to make me realize
how small I'd become.

267
00:30:37,125 --> 00:30:38,125
Come help me!

268
00:30:42,541 --> 00:30:44,874
Better start helping them unload.

269
00:30:44,875 --> 00:30:46,500
Sure you won't come with me?

270
00:30:48,666 --> 00:30:50,666
Like it better being a low man.

271
00:30:53,083 --> 00:30:54,375
I liked it too.

272
00:31:33,833 --> 00:31:35,375
Change your mind?

273
00:31:39,708 --> 00:31:41,458
To replace the ones Theo lent me.

274
00:31:43,041 --> 00:31:45,833
You can, uh, set it up there.

275
00:31:58,625 --> 00:32:00,166
I hear you're building a home.

276
00:32:02,791 --> 00:32:05,833
Hagen started laying the
foundation a few days ago.

277
00:32:07,666 --> 00:32:09,583
When he laid the cornerstone...

278
00:32:11,541 --> 00:32:16,166
he asked the gods to keep our love
strong, as long as the home stood.

279
00:32:17,833 --> 00:32:19,250
I'm happy for you.

280
00:32:21,708 --> 00:32:24,791
I always thought his kindness
was what love felt like.

281
00:32:28,125 --> 00:32:29,916
But when he said it, I felt ill.

282
00:32:31,750 --> 00:32:33,000
I felt like...

283
00:32:39,166 --> 00:32:40,541
Why are you telling me this?

284
00:32:44,750 --> 00:32:45,833
I...

285
00:33:07,041 --> 00:33:08,458
Come with me.

286
00:33:10,833 --> 00:33:12,250
Come with me to Númenor.

287
00:33:20,541 --> 00:33:23,457
Low men of Pelargir. Salutations.

288
00:33:23,458 --> 00:33:25,915
I'm Theo. Son of Bronwyn.

289
00:33:25,916 --> 00:33:27,665
Bring the surveyor's equipment.

290
00:33:27,666 --> 00:33:29,041
Perhaps you didn't hear.

291
00:33:29,875 --> 00:33:33,165
This is Theo. His mother was Bronwyn.

292
00:33:33,166 --> 00:33:35,583
Of course she was. And who are you?

293
00:33:36,208 --> 00:33:37,707
He's the leader of half the colony.

294
00:33:37,708 --> 00:33:40,582
Here to help me uphold the
agreement we made with your Queen.

295
00:33:40,583 --> 00:33:42,125
Agreement's changed.

296
00:33:42,958 --> 00:33:45,082
We'll build the watchtower
in sight of the river.

297
00:33:45,083 --> 00:33:46,916
Fell a few houses if we need to.

298
00:33:47,833 --> 00:33:49,791
It's a disgrace, the
state this place is in.

299
00:33:50,500 --> 00:33:51,750
Is that Kemen?

300
00:33:55,416 --> 00:33:56,625
Isildur?

301
00:33:59,500 --> 00:34:02,791
Your sister will be so
pleased to hear we found you.

302
00:34:06,708 --> 00:34:07,999
I never gave up hope,

303
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:11,250
even when everyone said
there were no survivors left.

304
00:34:11,916 --> 00:34:14,583
There wouldn't be, if not for Berek.

305
00:34:19,166 --> 00:34:20,582
I trust there's room on the ship.

306
00:34:20,583 --> 00:34:21,999
Plenty.

307
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:23,750
Then one more should be no trouble.

308
00:34:38,458 --> 00:34:40,208
No passage for low men.

309
00:34:42,458 --> 00:34:45,874
I survived an eruption.
My sister's a guild member.

310
00:34:45,875 --> 00:34:48,500
My father, Post-Captain
to Queen-regent Míriel.

311
00:34:50,333 --> 00:34:51,790
Surely an exception can be made.

312
00:34:51,791 --> 00:34:53,499
I'm afraid you're mistaken.

313
00:34:53,500 --> 00:34:55,290
My father is now King.

314
00:34:55,291 --> 00:34:58,916
And yours... is wanted for treason.

315
00:35:01,041 --> 00:35:02,415
It might've been worse.

316
00:35:02,416 --> 00:35:04,958
If I'd had it my way,
the old fool'd be dead.

317
00:35:06,791 --> 00:35:08,624
I saved your life, you miserable...

318
00:35:08,625 --> 00:35:10,708
Shall I have them slaughter the horse?

319
00:35:11,666 --> 00:35:13,500
These people do look hungry.

320
00:35:21,625 --> 00:35:25,750
Disrespect me again, and you
really will be lost to Middle-earth.

321
00:35:28,666 --> 00:35:29,916
Hear this now.

322
00:35:31,000 --> 00:35:33,755
Pelargir is no longer
a colony of Númenor

323
00:35:33,756 --> 00:35:36,082
but a fortress for its soldiers.

324
00:35:36,083 --> 00:35:37,749
And I am its Commander.

325
00:35:37,750 --> 00:35:39,999
Any low man wishing to remain here

326
00:35:40,000 --> 00:35:43,582
will deliver a regular allotment of
timber from the surrounding forests

327
00:35:43,583 --> 00:35:46,290
for the construction
of His Majesty's armada.

328
00:35:46,291 --> 00:35:49,457
What about the supplies you
promised? The food for winter?

329
00:35:49,458 --> 00:35:51,707
No timber, no supplies.

330
00:35:51,708 --> 00:35:53,845
But I'm certain that
won't be a problem for you.

331
00:35:53,846 --> 00:35:56,375
After all, they're only trees.

332
00:36:27,750 --> 00:36:29,791
She-Elf turned herself in.

333
00:36:31,291 --> 00:36:32,625
Leave us.

334
00:36:34,583 --> 00:36:35,666
Leave us.

335
00:36:41,416 --> 00:36:43,250
I accept your terms, Uruk.

336
00:36:45,125 --> 00:36:46,791
I have what Sauron seeks.

337
00:36:47,750 --> 00:36:51,500
End this slaughter and
I will do as you asked.

338
00:36:52,125 --> 00:36:54,208
I will help you destroy him.

339
00:36:54,833 --> 00:36:58,875
How do you expect to destroy
Sauron without your Ring?

340
00:37:04,541 --> 00:37:09,125
It would seem, even wounds
that have endured an age,

341
00:37:09,791 --> 00:37:11,875
can sometimes yet be healed.

342
00:37:17,125 --> 00:37:18,374
Adar.

343
00:37:18,375 --> 00:37:22,916
When last I looked like this,
I was known by another name.

344
00:37:23,875 --> 00:37:25,166
What was it?

345
00:37:26,666 --> 00:37:30,291
A meaningless name. A name I was given.

346
00:37:34,625 --> 00:37:37,125
Adar is the name I earned.

347
00:37:45,916 --> 00:37:47,583
Help me earn it back.

348
00:37:57,875 --> 00:37:58,875
Take it.

349
00:38:00,208 --> 00:38:02,333
Help me vanquish Sauron with it.

350
00:38:03,708 --> 00:38:09,333
And I swear to you, I will
recall my children to Mordor.

351
00:38:09,958 --> 00:38:12,833
Never to make war on Middle-earth again.

352
00:38:14,125 --> 00:38:19,166
I have slain more of your
children than any Elf alive.

353
00:38:20,041 --> 00:38:22,041
I forgive you.

354
00:38:23,791 --> 00:38:26,958
No more flames, and no more darkness.

355
00:38:27,708 --> 00:38:30,749
Let this Ring heal the
rift between Elf and Uruk.

356
00:38:34,291 --> 00:38:37,540
Let us create a lasting
peace in Middle-earth.

357
00:38:37,541 --> 00:38:39,041
Now and forever.

358
00:39:09,775 --> 00:39:10,833
What happened?

359
00:39:10,834 --> 00:39:13,499
We found Sauron, Lord-father.

360
00:39:13,500 --> 00:39:17,374
He tried to make Glüg
betray you, but he resisted.

361
00:39:17,375 --> 00:39:19,291
So Sauron did this.

362
00:39:20,208 --> 00:39:22,749
The others are pursuing him now.

363
00:39:22,750 --> 00:39:24,333
Forgive me, child.

364
00:39:26,416 --> 00:39:27,833
It's too late.

365
00:39:28,375 --> 00:39:29,958
It is never too late.

366
00:39:31,208 --> 00:39:33,082
Not even for me.

367
00:39:33,083 --> 00:39:35,207
And not for you, my son.

368
00:39:39,500 --> 00:39:40,916
It's too late.

369
00:40:16,541 --> 00:40:17,707
Galadriel.

370
00:40:55,291 --> 00:40:58,040
My... children...

371
00:40:58,041 --> 00:41:00,125
They are not children anymore.

372
00:41:24,083 --> 00:41:27,916
What orders, Lord Sauron?

373
00:41:29,291 --> 00:41:30,750
Raze Eregion.

374
00:41:32,333 --> 00:41:33,999
Leave no Elf alive.

375
00:41:35,333 --> 00:41:37,000
But bring me their leaders.

376
00:41:38,541 --> 00:41:40,332
Hail Sauron!

377
00:41:40,333 --> 00:41:43,540
Hail the new Dark Lord!

378
00:41:43,541 --> 00:41:45,000
Hail Lord Sauron!

379
00:41:48,083 --> 00:41:50,915
Hail Lord Sauron!

380
00:41:53,833 --> 00:41:55,125
All this...

381
00:41:57,000 --> 00:41:59,000
was your design from the beginning.

382
00:41:59,666 --> 00:42:04,166
Please. You think too much of me.

383
00:42:06,291 --> 00:42:10,000
The road goes ever winding.

384
00:42:10,500 --> 00:42:13,458
Not even I can see all its paths.

385
00:42:27,208 --> 00:42:30,458
It is even more beautiful than
Celebrimbor led me to believe.

386
00:42:38,541 --> 00:42:39,541
Give it to me.

387
00:42:43,833 --> 00:42:46,750
Give me your Ring... and the Nine.

388
00:42:47,750 --> 00:42:49,665
It is not my wish to harm you.

389
00:42:49,666 --> 00:42:51,458
Do you wish to heal me?

390
00:42:52,375 --> 00:42:56,499
I wish to heal... all Middle-earth.

391
00:42:56,500 --> 00:42:58,416
As you have Eregion?

392
00:43:28,333 --> 00:43:29,624
Bring it down.

393
00:43:33,458 --> 00:43:34,958
And pull!

394
00:43:50,875 --> 00:43:51,915
- No, Uruk!
- No!

395
00:43:51,916 --> 00:43:54,624
That is the full record
of Celebrimbor's works.

396
00:43:54,625 --> 00:43:57,000
The wisdom of all who
ever dwelt in this place.

397
00:43:58,166 --> 00:44:01,458
Its value is beyond
jewels or even blood.

398
00:44:01,958 --> 00:44:04,875
Take our lives. But
leave it be, I beg you.

399
00:44:09,208 --> 00:44:10,875
Cowardly traitors!

400
00:44:29,000 --> 00:44:30,290
Wait!

401
00:44:30,291 --> 00:44:33,291
Lord Sauron wanted
their leaders unharmed.

402
00:45:16,333 --> 00:45:17,375
Galadriel,

403
00:45:18,916 --> 00:45:22,707
surely you of all Elves must understand

404
00:45:22,708 --> 00:45:27,375
that to find the light, we
must first touch the darkness.

405
00:45:30,291 --> 00:45:32,874
We are not alike. We never were.

406
00:45:32,875 --> 00:45:34,958
It was just another of your illusions.

407
00:45:36,375 --> 00:45:37,666
Not all of it.

408
00:46:06,250 --> 00:46:07,583
Fighting at your side,

409
00:46:08,708 --> 00:46:11,333
I felt, if I could just
hold on to that feeling.

410
00:46:26,541 --> 00:46:30,291
They could no longer distinguish
me from the evil I was fighting.

411
00:46:47,041 --> 00:46:49,125
Are they not the seeds you planted?

412
00:47:16,708 --> 00:47:17,916
I see you.

413
00:47:28,416 --> 00:47:29,833
I know your mind.

414
00:47:37,583 --> 00:47:39,041
The door is still open.

415
00:47:42,458 --> 00:47:44,000
The door is shut.

416
00:48:34,625 --> 00:48:37,083
I would have placed a
crown upon your head.

417
00:48:38,666 --> 00:48:40,874
I would never have rested

418
00:48:40,875 --> 00:48:44,166
until all Middle-earth had
been brought to its knees,

419
00:48:46,375 --> 00:48:48,832
to worship the light of its Queen.

420
00:48:54,083 --> 00:48:57,708
The free peoples of Middle-earth

421
00:48:59,166 --> 00:49:03,165
will always resist you.

422
00:49:35,166 --> 00:49:36,666
The Rings are mine.

423
00:49:51,708 --> 00:49:52,957
Dwarves.

424
00:50:10,125 --> 00:50:11,290
Come on. Get off me.

425
00:50:11,291 --> 00:50:12,500
Durin.

426
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:16,000
No!

427
00:50:16,833 --> 00:50:19,125
The Prince is in mourning.

428
00:50:21,250 --> 00:50:22,458
Move it!

429
00:50:25,500 --> 00:50:27,041
Give me your Ring.

430
00:50:43,708 --> 00:50:48,000
Galadriel. Your Ring.

431
00:51:09,750 --> 00:51:13,250
You wish to heal Middle-earth?

432
00:51:18,083 --> 00:51:19,457
Heal yourself.

433
00:51:50,208 --> 00:51:52,415
We are overwhelmed, Lord Sauron.

434
00:51:52,416 --> 00:51:55,124
The Dwarves are securing
the Elves' retreat.

435
00:51:55,125 --> 00:51:57,458
If we pursue, many Uruks...

436
00:52:40,750 --> 00:52:44,166
These are not merely wounds of the body.

437
00:52:45,208 --> 00:52:49,791
Her very immortal spirit is
being drawn into the shadow realm.

438
00:52:51,958 --> 00:52:57,958
By the light of the Elder King,

439
00:52:58,666 --> 00:53:02,374
I command all darkness
to depart from thee...

440
00:53:14,791 --> 00:53:16,915
By the light of the Elder King,

441
00:53:16,916 --> 00:53:20,291
I command all darkness
to depart from thee...

442
00:53:23,375 --> 00:53:24,791
We're losing her.

443
00:53:25,458 --> 00:53:28,625
The darkness is too
powerful. I cannot save her.

444
00:53:35,625 --> 00:53:36,750
I can.

445
00:53:43,375 --> 00:53:44,541
We can.

446
00:54:44,083 --> 00:54:45,416
We'll have to fix it.

447
00:54:50,125 --> 00:54:51,458
After my family...

448
00:54:57,041 --> 00:54:58,791
Mr. Burrows sat me down.

449
00:55:00,916 --> 00:55:03,000
Told me, "Some things can't be fixed.

450
00:55:05,416 --> 00:55:10,833
"Some things lost are lost forever.

451
00:55:25,375 --> 00:55:28,208
"No matter how hard we fight...

452
00:55:41,500 --> 00:55:43,333
How much it hurts...

453
00:55:50,041 --> 00:55:52,666
Or how much our hearts yearn...

454
00:56:00,708 --> 00:56:02,708
To put them back together...

455
00:56:09,250 --> 00:56:12,250
'Cause this world's so
much bigger than any of us.

456
00:56:26,208 --> 00:56:29,833
And sometimes the winds blowin'
against us are just too strong.

457
00:56:36,833 --> 00:56:38,916
At those times," Mr. Burrows said,

458
00:56:42,375 --> 00:56:43,958
"we've just got to accept it.

459
00:56:47,875 --> 00:56:50,625
What's broke is broke and won't fix.

460
00:56:55,500 --> 00:57:00,916
And all anybody can do is
try and build something new."

461
00:57:18,750 --> 00:57:20,875
Don't be a stranger now.

462
00:57:25,458 --> 00:57:27,125
Thank you kindly, Grand-Elf.

463
00:57:28,166 --> 00:57:29,291
Huh.

464
00:57:31,791 --> 00:57:33,875
Why don't you grab something else?

465
00:57:39,458 --> 00:57:40,791
Goodbye, Grand-Elf.

466
00:57:47,458 --> 00:57:48,458
Grandelf?

467
00:57:50,375 --> 00:57:52,083
They've never seen an Elf before.

468
00:57:52,916 --> 00:57:54,416
Never even left home before.

469
00:57:55,000 --> 00:57:57,750
Right. I tried to help 'em pack, but...

470
00:57:58,750 --> 00:58:00,832
it's their first migration,

471
00:58:00,833 --> 00:58:03,291
and they haven't the
foggiest what to bring.

472
00:58:05,833 --> 00:58:07,416
And what to leave.

473
00:58:14,208 --> 00:58:15,791
If I had my druthers, we...

474
00:58:20,041 --> 00:58:22,000
We'd walk the wastes of this world.

475
00:58:24,333 --> 00:58:27,790
Eatin' snails and beetles
till the sun run out of days,

476
00:58:27,791 --> 00:58:33,000
but it's high time I walked
my path, and you walked yours.

477
00:58:37,291 --> 00:58:39,916
We are very different creatures, Nori.

478
00:58:41,416 --> 00:58:42,958
When all is said and done.

479
00:58:45,375 --> 00:58:47,375
Not so different at all, if you ask me.

480
01:00:35,208 --> 01:00:37,625
It was all a test, wasn't it?

481
01:00:38,750 --> 01:00:40,333
Another one of your riddles.

482
01:00:41,625 --> 01:00:44,750
I was meant to choose
friendship over power.

483
01:00:46,208 --> 01:00:47,750
I was meant to help them.

484
01:00:48,958 --> 01:00:51,958
I was meant to find this.

485
01:00:57,166 --> 01:00:59,291
A wizard does not find his staff.

486
01:01:01,041 --> 01:01:02,791
It finds him.

487
01:01:07,541 --> 01:01:08,875
Like his name.

488
01:01:22,541 --> 01:01:23,958
Gandalf.

489
01:01:28,083 --> 01:01:30,416
That's what they're going
to call me, isn't it?

490
01:01:32,333 --> 01:01:34,541
Now let the song begin.

491
01:01:37,958 --> 01:01:39,583
Let us sing together.

492
01:01:41,041 --> 01:01:44,083
Merry dol derry dol Ring a ding dillo

493
01:01:44,666 --> 01:01:50,040
Sandflies in the grass
Bees around the willow

494
01:01:50,041 --> 01:01:52,290
Now let the song begin

495
01:01:52,291 --> 01:01:54,166
Let us sing together

496
01:01:54,833 --> 01:02:00,415
Of sun, stars, moon and
mist, Rain and cloudy weather

497
01:02:00,416 --> 01:02:05,499
Light on the budding
leaf Dew on the feather

498
01:02:05,500 --> 01:02:10,541
Wind on the open hills
Bells on the heather

499
01:02:11,333 --> 01:02:16,374
Old Tom Bombadil Is a merry fellow

500
01:02:16,375 --> 01:02:21,250
Bright blue his jacket is
And his boots are yellow

501
01:02:21,958 --> 01:02:27,041
Reeds by the shady
pool Lilies on the water

502
01:02:27,666 --> 01:02:32,875
Old Tom Bombadil And the River-daughter

503
01:03:04,625 --> 01:03:06,041
Eregion has fallen.

504
01:03:07,250 --> 01:03:10,916
The survivors have fled
to a valley North of here.

505
01:03:12,541 --> 01:03:13,957
And Elrond?

506
01:03:13,958 --> 01:03:15,208
He led them.

507
01:03:18,291 --> 01:03:19,708
Dispatch word.

508
01:03:20,750 --> 01:03:25,083
Tell him, Khazad-dûm stands
ready to offer aid once more.

509
01:03:25,833 --> 01:03:28,416
We have troubles of our own, my love.

510
01:03:31,083 --> 01:03:34,958
Your father's passing
has left us in a tangle.

511
01:03:36,416 --> 01:03:40,250
The Lords of the Blue
Mountains paid him vast tributes

512
01:03:41,500 --> 01:03:43,290
and they're demanding to collect.

513
01:03:43,291 --> 01:03:44,957
But there's more.

514
01:03:44,958 --> 01:03:49,250
Rumors fly that you were not
your father's preferred heir.

515
01:03:49,916 --> 01:03:53,500
That some of the other
Dwarf-lords are advancing claims.

516
01:03:54,875 --> 01:03:58,916
And, um, your brother seems
to be gathering support.

517
01:04:22,291 --> 01:04:23,500
Pity.

518
01:04:24,166 --> 01:04:27,124
I've never known you to
be such peaceable company.

519
01:04:27,125 --> 01:04:30,291
I believe I was growing
accustomed to it.

520
01:04:36,833 --> 01:04:38,000
Rest.

521
01:04:38,750 --> 01:04:40,541
We are safe here.

522
01:04:46,958 --> 01:04:50,583
- What is this place?
- A sanctuary.

523
01:04:51,333 --> 01:04:56,291
Protected... by the Elven Rings.

524
01:05:21,875 --> 01:05:22,958
Commander.

525
01:05:23,708 --> 01:05:24,791
Arondir.

526
01:05:29,416 --> 01:05:32,708
I have gathered the others, High
King. They await your decision.

527
01:05:37,125 --> 01:05:40,583
Sauron's armies are
roving across Eriador.

528
01:05:41,791 --> 01:05:45,166
All Middle-earth is within
his reach now. Even Lindon.

529
01:05:46,250 --> 01:05:50,791
We must decide whether to attack
and bring the fight to him...

530
01:05:51,666 --> 01:05:54,583
or to fall back, to
prepare our defenses.

531
01:05:57,250 --> 01:05:58,750
The sword or the shield.

532
01:06:01,125 --> 01:06:03,540
Many of Eregion's bravest fell.

533
01:06:03,541 --> 01:06:06,915
The few who survived are all
but broken. In body or spirit.

534
01:06:06,916 --> 01:06:09,708
They have little strength
left with which to fight.

535
01:06:10,250 --> 01:06:12,125
They barely had strength to flee.

536
01:06:14,583 --> 01:06:17,208
What course would you
advise, Commander Galadriel?

537
01:06:29,833 --> 01:06:31,750
I would remember the counsel

538
01:06:33,041 --> 01:06:37,125
of our dear friend, Celebrimbor,

539
01:06:38,833 --> 01:06:41,083
Greatest of Elven-smiths.

540
01:06:45,583 --> 01:06:47,333
And remind our people...

541
01:06:49,000 --> 01:06:53,374
that it is not strength
that overcomes darkness,

542
01:06:53,375 --> 01:06:54,750
but light.

543
01:07:07,666 --> 01:07:10,083
And the sun yet shines.

544
01:08:36,501 --> 01:08:41,501
